# --- The build plan stays out of git ---
# BIOGENT_PLAN.md is local-only: it contains pilot-researcher data arrangements
# and the discovery-funnel design, neither of which belongs on GitHub.
#
# By EXACT NAME, deliberately not a glob. A pattern like *_PLAN.md would also
# swallow any other plan doc this repo later tracks -- which is exactly the bug
# the main BioGent repo already hit once, when a broad "planning" ignore block
# hid ARCHITECTURE.md and PRODUCTION_PLAN.md and left AGENTS.md pointing at
# files that were missing from a fresh clone.
#
# .gitignore rather than .git/info/exclude (which is what the plan file itself
# suggests): exclude is per-clone and unversioned, so cloning onto a second
# machine and forgetting to re-add it is one `git add -A` away from publishing
# the plan. This line travels with the repo. The cost is leaking the filename,
# not its contents.
BIOGENT_PLAN.md
.claude

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.log

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- R ---
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
# renv caches the packages themselves; only the lockfile is tracked.
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/staging/

# --- Research data (never commit real datasets) ---
# Pilot researcher data is unpublished and belongs to them. Test datasets,
# marker CSVs, .h5ad and .rds files all live here and stay here.
data/
uploads/
*.h5ad
*.rds
*.h5
*.loom

# --- Generated analysis output ---
# Eval REPORTS are tracked on purpose (see evals/reports/) -- these are the
# intermediate artifacts a run produces, which are not.
scratch/
figures/
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.pdf

# --- Docker ---
*.pid

# --- OS clutter ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Editor / IDE ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- Private MD Files ---
BIOGENT_PLAN.md
